# Store and check out every text file with LF, regardless of who clones the repo.
#
# This lives in the repo on purpose: Git for Windows ships core.autocrlf=true at system
# level, and per-developer config does not travel with a clone. Without this, files get
# committed with CRLF, diffs report every line as changed, and a CRLF shell script
# copied into a Linux image fails with a confusing "\r: not found".
* text=auto eol=lf

# Never line-ending convert binaries or the lockfile.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
package-lock.json -text
